.TH MAKE:POLYGLOT-PARTIAL 1 "October 2026" "SPP Framework" "SPP CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
make:polyglot-partial \- Scaffolds a new external polyglot view partial service file for any registered language
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B php spp.php make:polyglot-partial
\fIFilename.ext\fR [\fB\-\-lang=\fR\fIlanguage\fR] [\fB\-\-app=\fR\fIAppName\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B make:polyglot-partial
generates standalone external service partials that execute through SPP's Universal Polyglot 2.0 bridge subsystem. Partials can be written in any language registered in \fILanguageRegistry\fR, including Python, Node.js, Go, Rust, Zig, Ruby, Elixir, Lua, Java, C#, or custom in-process DSLs.
.PP
Generated partials conform to SPP's zero-inline-HTML standard and can be seamlessly consumed by ViewControllers via \fBrenderPolyglotPartial()\fR or embedded within Blade templates using \fB@polyglot()\fR directives.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B Filename.ext
Name of the partial file to create with appropriate extension (e.g., \fIchart.py\fR, \fIwidget.go\fR, \fIrule.calc\fR).
.TP
.BR \-\-lang =\fIlanguage\fR
Explicit language identifier (e.g. \fIpython\fR, \fInode\fR, \fIgo\fR, \fIrust\fR, \fIformula\fR). Inferred from extension if omitted.
.TP
.BR \-\-app =\fIAppName\fR
Application context where the partial should be created. If specified, targets \fIsrc/<AppName>/services/polyglot/\fR; otherwise defaults to \fIservices/polyglot/\fR.
.SH UNDER THE HOOD
.IP \(bu 2
Resolves driver configuration via \fISPP\\Core\\Polyglot\\LanguageRegistry\fR.
.IP \(bu 2
Ensures target service directories exist.
.IP \(bu 2
Generates idiomatic input decoding and output formatting stubs in the requested language.
